Law texts

The texts in this repository are the Acts, Ordinances and Regulations of Balochistan (Pakistan) as published on the
Balochistan Code (balochistancode.gob.pk) by the Law and Parliamentary Affairs Department, Government of Balochistan
("Copyright, All rights reserved by Law & parliamentary affairs department Balochistan"). The site states no terms
of use and no licence for reuse.

- Copyright: the Copyright Ordinance, 1962 (Ordinance No. XXXIV of 1962), s. 57(1) begins "The following acts shall
  not constitute an infringement of copyright, namely:" and clause (q) reads: "the reproduction or publication of__
  (i) any matter which has been published in any official Gazette, or the report of any committee, commission,
  council, board or other like body appointed by the Government unless the reproduction or publication of such
  matter or report is prohibited by the Government". The laws of Balochistan are published in the Balochistan
  Gazette (the footnotes of these texts record the Gazette publication), and no prohibition by the Government of
  reproducing them was found. The texts are reproduced without change to their wording; only the arrangement (one
  file per section or Schedule, one paragraph per line) is Lexifina's.
- Limits of that basis: where a text incorporates later amendments, that arrangement and the footnotes (kept in
  data/amendments.csv) are the department's. Section 57(1)(q)(i) covers matter published in the Gazette; it does not
  in terms cover the department's arrangement and footnotes, which record facts (which law changed which words).
- The texts are not the authoritative text: the laws as published in the Balochistan Gazette are.

